WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.501
-Our next guest
is a Tony-nominated

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.037
and Emmy-winning actress

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.605
you know from her work on the
hit series "Abbott Elementary,"

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:07.373
which airs
Wednesday nights on ABC.

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:08.574
Let's take a look.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.810
-Ooh, this look is a slay,
Mrs. Howard.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:13.479
It's giving grade-A baddie.
-[ Gasps ]

00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:16.916
-Well, period to that.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.319
I could never do this
on my own every day,

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:22.321
but it's nice to see
what I could look like.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:25.125
Thank you. Oh!

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:30.329
Gerald, honey,
grab your gaiters

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.064
'cause we are
going out tonight.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:35.268
'Cause Mama looks good, baby.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.903
-Please welcome
back to the show

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.471
Sheryl Lee Ralph, everybody.

00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:42.475
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:52.385 align:start size:6% position:94% line:0%
♪♪

00:00:52.452 --> 00:01:02.295 align:start size:6% position:94% line:0%
♪♪

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:05.164
Welcome back!
-Thank you!

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.468
-Mama looks good in the clip,
Mama looks good here.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:09.969
-Oh, God, I love you.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.904
-It's just wonderful.
-Thank you very much.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.940
-I mean, always,
always looks fantastic.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:16.008
I'm so happy to have you back.
And I'm so happy to have

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.477
"Abbott Elementary" back.
This is season three.

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:19.845
Delayed.
-Ahh!

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.815
[ Cheers and applause ]
-The delayed gratification.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.216
This was -- Everything
was shut down

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:26.385
because of the writers strike
and then the SAG strike.

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:28.354
It just must be
so lovely to be back

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.455
with this wonderful
cast and crew.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.823
-Oh, my God.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.292
You know, it was so interesting,
all of that time off --

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.594
which was necessary.
-Yes.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.863
-The strikes were worth it.
-Absolutely.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:40.999
-Go, workers! Yeah!
They were worth it.

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:48.074
But to get back and just be
there with the best cast on TV,

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:52.478
oh, it is just a blessing,
and I feel good every day.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:56.515
I don't know about that 5:30
in the morning call, but, uh...

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.183
-They start you early.
Let's be honest.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.220
They start you early.
And no respect for the fact

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.487
that you're here
in New York City right now.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.223
You're gonna get
on a flight after this.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.224
You're going to go back to LA.
Got to go to work tomorrow.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.627
-Got to go to work tomorrow.
But you have to know, Seth,

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:14.633
I am making a great sacrifice
being here with you today.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.703
Oh, I am, because, Seth,

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:22.308
there is a really big star

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:25.711
guest-starring
on the show this week.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:28.915
They only had three hours.
Just three hours.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:32.919
-Ah!
-Hit it and quit it.

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:34.887
And I've said to them,
"Guess what --

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:37.323
I told Seth yes."

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.491
-I'm so -- I'm already
so disappointed

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:41.460
that people are going to be
watching this big star

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.597
and every person is going
to be like, "She chose Seth?"

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:47.299
-[ Laughs ] Yes, I did.
-Thank you.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.334
-You have to see Seth
in a crowd.

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:51.771
We were there
at the Emmys, right?

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:56.208
And when Seth is there,
Seth is like a charming magnet.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.677
-Oh, thank you.
-And all the guy-guys,

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:00.780
they all want
to crowd around Seth

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:02.181
and just look at Seth.

00:03:02.247 --> 00:03:04.683
And it's like,
"I want to be like Seth."

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.886
-Oh, my God.
-"Seth is a good guy."

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.389
And Seth is a good guy.
-Oh, my God. I mean...

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.724
[ Cheers and applause ]
You are...

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.460
I've always known
you are a fantastic actor,

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.562
but to see
what a great liar you are...

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:18.063
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.499
Now, I -- you know,

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:21.500
you said it's the best cast,
and I truly believe it.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.337
And I am sometimes
so jealous of the writers

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:27.640
that get to write
for performers like yourself.

00:03:27.706 --> 00:03:29.709
Barbara, your character,
mixes up celebrity names.

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:32.745
This was another gift
you bestowed upon the writers.

00:03:32.811 --> 00:03:35.414
This is something
you actually do.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.017
They heard you doing this and
then gave it to the character.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:39.519
Is this true?

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:41.053
-[ Sighs ]

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.387
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:45.724
Okay, I will just say
this to you.

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:50.363
When you hear
the name Orlando Bloom,

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:53.532
tell me you don't see
big Black football player.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.301
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:56.969
-I do, yeah.
-Thank you!

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.705
-No, it does seem
like a left tackle.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.005
That does seem like
a left tackle name.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:02.275
-I'm telling you!
When I heard...

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:07.112
I knew for years
that Darren Star

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:10.049
was a young Black influencer.

00:04:10.115 --> 00:04:11.650
I knew it.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.986
When I was introduced
to Darren Star,

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:17.056
I was like, "Well,
where's Darren Star?"

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:21.060
I felt so bad to realize,
"Oh, my God,

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.396
this is not the man
I thought it was."

00:04:23.462 --> 00:04:26.531
But I come by it naturally
and honestly,

00:04:26.598 --> 00:04:28.301
and those are my mistakes.

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.903
And why it ended up in the show?

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.905
Mm, mm, mm.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.206
But it was funny.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:35.507
-There you go. It is funny.
-It's funny.

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:36.743
-It's funny every time.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.744
The season premiere
is about Career Day.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:41.346
You did not -- I would have
assumed, based on your talents,

00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:44.016
that you knew at a young age
acting was your path,

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:47.052
but you actually thought maybe
you were going to be a doctor.

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:49.155
-You know,
I'm an immigrant's child,

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:52.891
and most immigrants, when their
children are born in America,

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:54.960
they want you to be great.

00:04:55.027 --> 00:04:57.463
My mother was so shocked

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.366
that Barack Obama
was the first Black president,

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.768
because she swore
it was gonna be me.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.603
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.140
-There you go. There you go.
She had high hopes.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.674
-Oh, my God!
-High hopes.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.310
-She just knew
it was gonna be me.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:14.480
So when I went to college --
Rutgers -- I was --

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:16.449
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you!

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:18.617
Yes, yes!

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:21.120
On the banks
of the old Raritan.

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.289
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:27.593
So, when I got to Rutgers,
I was a pre-med student, right?

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.428
And I thought
this was gonna be it.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:32.331
But, you know, when you're
in these certain classes,

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:35.034
okay, you have to dissect
and cut things up.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.203
And there, placed
in front of me,

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.438
is a huge hare --

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.440
H-A-R-E.
-Okay.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:46.112
-Which is basically
the Easter Bunny on steroids.

00:05:46.178 --> 00:05:48.113
-Did you get an Easter Bunny
vibe off it?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.916
-Oh, my God, when I saw...

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.451
Well, actually, I saw this coat

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.787
that I really wanted
when I was small.

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:56.455
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.522 --> 00:06:00.693
But anyway, there it was
on the tray,

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:03.229
and they gave me
my first scalpel

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:05.064
in a nice blue velvet thing.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.432
And I took it out
and I was like,

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:09.435
"I am not cutting up
the Easter Bunny!

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:11.270
That's not happening!"

00:06:11.336 --> 00:06:13.806
So, I immediately
leave that class

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.808
and I go straight
to the registrar,

00:06:15.874 --> 00:06:18.277
and I am going to
become a lawyer.

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:23.549
Somehow I get in
the constitutional law class,

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:28.387
and this lady, tiny little lady
with her hair in a severe bun,

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:34.160
and she just went
on and on about the law...

00:06:34.226 --> 00:06:36.795
-It was a law class.
-It was a law -- Ah.

00:06:36.862 --> 00:06:38.497
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:44.470
-And I was like,
"Hell to the no, no, no."

00:06:44.536 --> 00:06:45.971
So, when I went back,

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:48.274
after giving the commencement
at Rutgers,

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:51.777
they said, "Constitutional law?

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:54.246
Tiny lady, hair in a severe bun?

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:57.015
Was that Ruth Bader Ginsburg?"

00:06:57.082 --> 00:07:01.721
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:01.787 --> 00:07:05.757
They did the math
and they were like, "Sheryl,

00:07:05.824 --> 00:07:09.595
you walked out on RBG."

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:14.467
And I was like,
"Oh, my God! Yes, I did!"

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:16.468
But anyway,
that's how it goes.

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:18.304
-It all worked out.
-Touch! Yes!

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:22.975
-And you did, by the way...
You were not...

00:07:23.042 --> 00:07:24.977
You were not
our first Black president,

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:26.511
but you did make
a little bit of history.

00:07:26.578 --> 00:07:29.214
I've talked about this before,
but a couple years back,

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:30.750
I presented you with the Emmy.
-Yes, you did.

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:33.285
-Me and Amy Poehler,
for Best Supporting.

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.487
-Yes.
-And this was...

00:07:35.554 --> 00:07:37.290
You were only the second.
Is that correct?

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:38.858
-I was only the second
woman in thirty--

00:07:38.925 --> 00:07:40.927
second Black woman in 35 years.

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:43.095
-In 35 years.
-To be nominated and win.

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:44.430
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:44.496 --> 00:07:46.198
-And then something
very cool happened,

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:49.034
which was --
again, two in 35 years,

00:07:49.101 --> 00:07:50.369
and then two in two years,

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:52.304
because this year
you're nominated again,

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:56.241
and our friend Ayo won, and you
got to celebrate with her.

00:07:56.308 --> 00:07:58.010
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:58.077 --> 00:07:59.779
And you knew her,
you worked with her.

00:07:59.845 --> 00:08:01.613
It must have been
a very special thing.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.048
-You know something?

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:05.050
My father would say
this all the time.

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:07.152
To be the first is wonderful.

00:08:07.219 --> 00:08:09.155
To be the second is great.

00:08:09.221 --> 00:08:10.990
But once there is
the first and second,

00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:12.824
what does it mean
if there's not a third?

00:08:12.891 --> 00:08:14.927
-There you go.
-So I was very happy

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:17.596
to be able to see her
take that win.

00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:21.433
I was like, "Go, Ayo.
You go, girl."

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.436
-We were very lucky to have you

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:26.538
at the Macy's Thanksgiving
Day Parade this year.

00:08:26.605 --> 00:08:29.007
You were our Mrs. Claus.
And a role --

00:08:29.074 --> 00:08:30.709
a role you were born to play.
-I was.

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:32.377
-Yes.
-And I am.

00:08:32.444 --> 00:08:35.848
And I'm telling you, when --
you should have seen kids' faces

00:08:35.915 --> 00:08:40.319
when they saw me,
they were like, "Oh, my God!"

00:08:40.385 --> 00:08:42.788
They were like,
"Hi, lady! Lady!"

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:44.456
Oh, my God.

00:08:44.523 --> 00:08:46.459
It was just so heartwarming.

00:08:46.525 --> 00:08:48.627
And adults were like,

00:08:48.694 --> 00:08:50.796
"That's Sheryl Lee Ralph."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:52.632
"That's Sheryl Lee Ralph."

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:54.767
Oh, it was --
it was just the best day.

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:56.135
And I didn't freeze
too much either.

00:08:56.201 --> 00:08:57.703
-That's good.
It wasn't too bad.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:58.971
-It wasn't too bad.
-There you go.

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:00.739
-You see what I did,
though, to Mrs. Claus?

00:09:00.805 --> 00:09:01.974
I had to zhuzh her up.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:04.076
I said, cock that hat
to the side, baby.

00:09:04.143 --> 00:09:06.579
-Yeah.
Let's get a little style.

00:09:06.645 --> 00:09:08.413
-Yeah.
-Yeah, let's get a little style.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.249
They have fashion
in the North Pole, too.

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:11.317
-Thank you!

00:09:11.383 --> 00:09:12.485
-What a delight
to have you back.

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:13.618
It is always
such a pleasure.

00:09:13.685 --> 00:09:14.787
Can't wait to see
the new season.

00:09:14.854 --> 00:09:16.856
-Mwah!
-Sheryl Lee Ralph, everybody.

00:09:16.922 --> 00:09:18.991
"Abbott Elementary" airs
Wednesday nights on ABC.

00:09:19.057 --> 00:09:20.426
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

